          "targetDoi": "10.1007/978-3-662-05330-0",
          "snippet": "The relation between the expansion amplitudes of the scattered and of the incident fields defines the T-matrix; thus, the scattering problem is reduced to the calculations of these coefficients through, e.g. the imposition of the boundary conditions across the surface of the particle, or by point matching numerically the fields at the surface [11,45]. T-matrix methods work best with objects that are highly symmetric in Fig.",
