          "snippet": "However, the situation becomes much more complex for non-spherical particles, e.g. elongated particles, optically anisotropic particles, and inhomogeneous particles [45]. Moreover, in optical trapping experiments complex objects from tens of nanometers to tens of micrometers are manipulated, and cells, biological structures, metallic, dielectric, or hybrid structures are often far from the two extreme regimes or from spherical shapes.",
